What qstack takes from pstack:

  - The architecture: a routing skill whose playbooks are copied into a
    todolist verbatim, short model-only principle leaf skills that are cited
    when they change a decision, a SessionStart hook that injects the routing
    mandate, and project playbooks that extend bundled ones by anchoring to
    quoted step text.
  - skills/principle-test-behavior-not-implementation and
    skills/principle-explain-the-number adapt pstack's principles of the
    same names.
  - skills/create-harness follows the shape of pstack's
    create-verification-skill and maintain-verification-skill (interview the
    repository, generate a launch, doctor, drive, evidence, and cleanup
    recipe, prove it by running it, keep it honest with a refresh pass),
    generalized from apps to rigs, stations, pipelines, and eval runners.

Everything else in qstack (the core loop, the lenses, the QA playbooks, the
other principles, the guard hook, the agents, the
references, and the scripts) is original to qstack.
